Description: Native Linux desktop file automation daemon and configuration utility
 Hazelux is a native Linux desktop file automation daemon and graphical
 configuration utility architected for Debian and Ubuntu derivatives,
 with primary optimization for Zorin OS. It continuously evaluates
 filesystem events against user-defined declarative rules to automate
 routine file organization tasks such as sorting, renaming, and cleaning.
